---
// no props
---
<main class="page">

  <!-- MASTHEAD -->
  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="masthead-left">
      <div class="kicker">v3 deck &middot; Merantix Berlin</div>
      <h1>Going from Outputs <em>to Outcomes.</em></h1>
    </div>
    <div class="masthead-right">
      <strong>Miguel Dias</strong><br>
      Independent VSM consultant<br>
      12 May 2026
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- LEDE -->
  <p class="lede">
    AI multiplies output, but it's not multiplying outcomes. How do we close the gap?
  </p>

  <!-- COVER IMAGE -->
  <figure class="editorial-figure">
    <img src="/images/2026-05-12/outputs-to-outcomes.jpg" alt="Miguel Dias presenting outputs to outcomes at Merantix Berlin" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>Outputs to Outcomes &middot; Merantix Berlin</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 01 — THE FIVE PROBLEMS                          -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s01">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">The five problems <em>nobody stopped talking about.</em></div>
        <p class="section-dek">Across the panel, the talks, and the coffee-line conversations at <a href="https://luma.com/prompt2026" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent); padding-bottom: 1px;">Prompt 2026</a>. Ranked loosely by how often they surfaced.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="challenges">

      <div class="challenge featured">
        <div class="challenge-label"><span class="dot"></span>Most cited</div>
        <h3>Output is multiplying. Outcomes aren&rsquo;t.</h3>
        <p>An engineer shipped five microservices with AI instead of one. Nobody pays per microservice. How do we know we&rsquo;re building the right things?</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 10px; font-size: 12px; font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-mute);">The exception that proved the rule: Intercom was the only talk that tied engineering effort to a single business metric &mdash; support cases resolved with the user&rsquo;s problem actually solved.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="challenge">
        <div class="challenge-label"><span class="dot"></span>Recurring</div>
        <h3>Picking what to build.</h3>
        <p>Getting the why and the what before the how. Working closer with customers to decide what actually matters.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="challenge">
        <div class="challenge-label"><span class="dot"></span>Recurring</div>
        <h3>Burnout and overload.</h3>
        <p>Context switching is up. More agents, more concurrent work. One CEO prescribed longer hours. Others pushed back.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="challenge">
        <div class="challenge-label"><span class="dot"></span>Recurring</div>
        <h3>Harness engineering <em style="font-weight: 400;">(the weeds of agents, PRs, CD).</em></h3>
        <p>Everyone is building a version of this: orchestration, guardrails, feature flags, evals, the loop that keeps agents shipping safely. Different names, same problem.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="challenge">
        <div class="challenge-label"><span class="dot"></span>Open problem</div>
        <h3>Quality is degrading.</h3>
        <p>More code, more bugs. Speakers named agents addressing quality <em>in production</em> as an unsolved problem.</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p class="challenges-footer">Everyone agreed outcomes matter more than output. Nobody said <em>how.</em><br><strong>But how do we get better outcomes?</strong></p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 02 — WHAT YOUR CTO WILL ASK NEXT QUARTER        -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s02">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">First of all, What will your CTO ask <em>end of quarter?</em></div>
        <p class="section-dek">Three-month window. The questions you&rsquo;ll get &mdash; and what you now have answers for.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accountability-map">
      <div class="am-row">
        <div class="am-target">&ldquo;Show me the AI ROI.&rdquo;</div>
        <div class="am-serves">More code &ne; more revenue. What&rsquo;s the conversion mechanism we&rsquo;re building?</div>
      </div>
      <div class="am-row">
        <div class="am-target">&ldquo;Are we delivering on our commitments?&rdquo;</div>
        <div class="am-serves">Can we ship what we promised to our biggest customers, on time? If not &mdash; where is it stuck, and why?</div>
      </div>
      <div class="am-row am-open">
        <div class="am-target">&ldquo;_______________________?&rdquo;</div>
        <div class="am-serves">What&rsquo;s your CTO actually asking? The right row beats both.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="am-caveat">Best guess at your CTO&rsquo;s quarterly. The point of the last row is the one we haven&rsquo;t guessed.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 03 — TWO ECONOMIES, ONE BUDGET                  -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s03">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Output vs Outcome Economics</div>
        <p class="section-dek">Local optimisation lives on Outputs. CTO targets are Outcomes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="economy-cols">
      <div class="economy-col output">
        <div class="economy-label">Output economics</div>
        <ul>
          <li>code shipped</li>
          <li>PRs merged</li>
          <li>deploys / week</li>
          <li>dev velocity</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="economy-col outcome">
        <div class="economy-label">Outcome economics</div>
        <ul>
          <li>revenue-bearing features</li>
          <li>bad bets killed early</li>
          <li>end-to-end TTM</li>
          <li>quality (fewer incidents, faster recovery)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="closing-line"><strong>&#9656; This deck moves the conversation to the right.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 04 — THE SCENARIO                               -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s04">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Example scenario, B2C</div>
        <p class="section-dek">Feature hit rate &mdash; what % of your bets paid off?</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="scenario-list">
      <li>~700 engineers &times; ~&euro;100k fully-loaded &asymp; <strong>~&euro;70M / yr</strong></li>
      <li>~100 features shipped per year</li>
      <li>~<strong>5&ndash;10</strong> generate significant revenue</li>
      <li>Lead time idea-to-production: <strong>???</strong> &mdash; Why&rsquo;s this the single most outcome-predicting metric?</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="scenario-impact">
      <div class="si-question"><em>Now &mdash; what if 5&ndash;10 became 15?</em></div>
      <div class="si-formula">5&ndash;10 extra winners &times; &euro;500k&ndash;1.5M each</div>
      <div class="si-number">&asymp; &euro;2.5M &ndash; &euro;15M / yr upside</div>
      <p class="si-note">Same team. Same budget. <strong>That&rsquo;s the prize this deck is chasing.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 05 — THREE WAYS TO MOVE THE NUMBER              -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s05">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">05</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Three ways to <em>move feature hit rate.</em></div>
        <p class="section-dek">What % of your bets paid off? What can we do to increase it?</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="options">

      <div class="option">
        <div class="option-letter">a.</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Hire more capacity.</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>coordination tax goes up</li>
            <li>Brooks ramp &mdash; new hires get worse before better</li>
            <li>onboarding dip on the team carrying them</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="option">
        <div class="option-letter">b.</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Same capacity &mdash; raise hit-rate and time to market.</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>moves the outcomes</li>
            <li>more money coming in, same capacity</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="option open-question">
        <div class="option-letter">c.</div>
        <div>
          <h3><em>Something else?</em></h3>
          <ul>
            <li>massive restructuring, team redesign&hellip;</li>
          </ul>
          <span class="punchline">&mdash; left open. Tell us what&rsquo;s on the table.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p class="option-footnote">
      Option (c) is the one we don&rsquo;t want to assume. Reorgs and restructuring often show up at growth-stage companies but rarely make the slide. Worth naming what&rsquo;s actually in scope before this conversation closes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 06 — TWO LEVERS                                 -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s06">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">06</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">What it takes to increase feature hit-rate:</div>
        <p class="section-dek">Same capacity, raise hit-rate and throughput = more revenue-bearing features. Two things need to move at the same time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="economy-cols">
      <div class="economy-col">
        <div class="economy-label">Lever 1: Faster time to market</div>
        <ul>
          <li>faster product discovery to experiment results</li>
          <li>engineering enables product leaders to experiment faster</li>
          <li>Look at: lead time from idea to production</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="economy-col outcome">
        <div class="economy-label">Lever 2: Quality</div>
        <ul>
          <li>more code = more quality problems</li>
          <li>no way around it except improve the system</li>
          <li>Look at: incidents, time to recover, rework eating capacity</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="closing-line">Both are measurable. Both respond to the same intervention: <strong>seeing the value stream clearly and managing it together.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 07 — 2-WEEK CADENCE INJECTS WASTE (Lever 1)     -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s07">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">07</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Example &mdash; how a <em>2-week cadence</em> injects waste.</div>
        <p class="section-dek">Lever 1 in action. One pattern &mdash; yours may be different. Mapping the value stream is how you find out.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gantt-wrap">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 720 300" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Gantt chart illustrating how a two-week sprint cadence injects waste: features stall at sprint boundaries between phases." style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif;">
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrowMuteG" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="4" orient="auto" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="#4a4640"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Sprint labels -->
        <text x="150" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="9.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">SPRINT 1</text>
        <text x="250" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="9.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">SPRINT 2</text>
        <text x="350" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="9.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">SPRINT 3</text>
        <text x="450" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="9.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">SPRINT 4</text>
        <text x="550" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="9.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">SPRINT 5</text>
        <text x="650" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="9.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">SPRINT 6</text>

        <!-- Time axis -->
        <line x1="100" y1="32" x2="700" y2="32" stroke="#4a4640" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#arrowMuteG)"/>
        <text x="704" y="36" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680">t</text>

        <!-- Sprint boundary dashed lines -->
        <line x1="200" y1="40" x2="200" y2="220" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
        <line x1="300" y1="40" x2="300" y2="220" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
        <line x1="400" y1="40" x2="400" y2="220" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
        <line x1="500" y1="40" x2="500" y2="220" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
        <line x1="600" y1="40" x2="600" y2="220" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>

        <!-- LANE 1: idea -->
        <text x="92" y="62" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">idea</text>
        <rect x="100" y="50" width="50" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>
        <rect x="150" y="50" width="50" height="18" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>

        <!-- LANE 2: spec -->
        <text x="92" y="90" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">spec</text>
        <rect x="200" y="78" width="70" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>
        <rect x="270" y="78" width="30" height="18" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>

        <!-- LANE 3: build -->
        <text x="92" y="118" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">build</text>
        <rect x="300" y="106" width="60" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>
        <rect x="360" y="106" width="40" height="18" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>

        <!-- LANE 4: release -->
        <text x="92" y="146" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">release</text>
        <rect x="400" y="134" width="40" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>
        <rect x="440" y="134" width="60" height="18" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>

        <!-- LANE 5: measure -->
        <text x="92" y="174" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">measure</text>
        <rect x="500" y="162" width="60" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>
        <rect x="560" y="162" width="40" height="18" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>

        <!-- LANE 6: decide (killed late) -->
        <text x="92" y="202" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">decide</text>
        <rect x="600" y="190" width="60" height="18" fill="#b8391f"/>
        <text x="666" y="203" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-style="italic" font-size="11" fill="#b8391f">&larr; killed</text>

        <!-- ANNOTATIONS -->
        <path d="M 175 230 L 175 240" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75"/>
        <text x="175" y="252" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-style="italic" font-size="11" fill="#8a8680">"waiting for next sprint"</text>

        <path d="M 470 230 L 470 240" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75"/>
        <text x="470" y="252" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-style="italic" font-size="11" fill="#8a8680">"CAB on Thursday"</text>

        <path d="M 630 218 L 630 240" fill="none" stroke="#b8391f" stroke-width="0.75"/>
        <text x="630" y="252" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-style="italic" font-size="11" fill="#b8391f">killed at month 3</text>

        <!-- Legend -->
        <line x1="40" y1="278" x2="680" y2="278" stroke="#d8d2c2" stroke-width="1"/>
        <rect x="100" y="288" width="16" height="10" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>
        <text x="122" y="297" font-size="10.5" fill="#4a4640">active work</text>
        <rect x="220" y="288" width="16" height="10" fill="none" stroke="#8a8680" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="2 2"/>
        <text x="242" y="297" font-size="10.5" fill="#4a4640">waiting (sprint boundary)</text>
        <rect x="430" y="288" width="16" height="10" fill="#b8391f"/>
        <text x="452" y="297" font-size="10.5" fill="#4a4640">killed late</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <p class="gantt-caption">
      One pattern. Yours may be different &mdash; <strong>mapping the value stream is how you find out</strong> which structural waste is actually costing you. <strong>Local dev speed is not the bottleneck;</strong> the cadence between phases is a cross-stream constraint.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE 08 — RELEASED FROM CADENCE + STACK BAND         -->
  <!-- ===================================================== -->
  <section id="s08">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">08</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Same stream &mdash; <em>released from the cadence.</em></div>
        <p class="section-dek">Same items, no sprint trap. Below the Gantt: where the measurement hooks would attach to a generic delivery stack.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gantt-wrap">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 720 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Compressed Gantt chart showing the same value stream released from sprint cadence, with measurement hooks at each transition." style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif;">
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrowMuteG2" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="4" orient="auto" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="#4a4640"/>
          </marker>
          <marker id="arrowAccentG2" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="4" orient="auto" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" fill="#b8391f"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- TOP: COMPRESSED GANTT -->
        <text x="100" y="20" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="9.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">CONTINUOUS FLOW</text>
        <line x1="100" y1="32" x2="700" y2="32" stroke="#4a4640" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#arrowMuteG2)"/>
        <text x="704" y="36" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680">t</text>

        <text x="92" y="62" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">idea</text>
        <rect x="100" y="50" width="34" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>

        <text x="92" y="90" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">spec</text>
        <rect x="134" y="78" width="50" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>

        <text x="92" y="118" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">build</text>
        <rect x="184" y="106" width="34" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>

        <text x="92" y="146" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">release</text>
        <rect x="218" y="134" width="34" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>

        <text x="92" y="174" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">measure</text>
        <rect x="252" y="162" width="22" height="18" fill="#1a1814" opacity="0.88"/>

        <text x="92" y="202" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1a1814">decide</text>
        <rect x="274" y="190" width="16" height="18" fill="#b8391f"/>
        <text x="298" y="203" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-style="italic" font-size="12" fill="#b8391f">&larr; kill at week 1</text>

        <!-- DIVIDER -->
        <line x1="40" y1="232" x2="680" y2="232" stroke="#d8d2c2" stroke-width="1"/>
        <text x="40" y="252" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10.5" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="2">YOUR DELIVERY STACK</text>

        <!-- STACK BAND -->
        <text x="100" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-weight="500" font-size="15" fill="#1a1814">Idea</text>
        <text x="100" y="298" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="1.5">tool</text>
        <line x1="125" y1="290" x2="175" y2="290" stroke="#1a1814" stroke-width="1.25" marker-end="url(#arrowMuteG2)"/>

        <text x="200" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-weight="500" font-size="15" fill="#1a1814">Spec</text>
        <text x="200" y="298" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="1.5">tool</text>
        <line x1="225" y1="290" x2="275" y2="290" stroke="#1a1814" stroke-width="1.25" marker-end="url(#arrowMuteG2)"/>

        <text x="300" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-weight="500" font-size="15" fill="#1a1814">Build</text>
        <text x="300" y="298" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="1.5">tool</text>
        <line x1="325" y1="290" x2="375" y2="290" stroke="#1a1814" stroke-width="1.25" marker-end="url(#arrowMuteG2)"/>

        <text x="400" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-weight="500" font-size="15" fill="#1a1814">Deploy</text>
        <text x="400" y="298" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="1.5">tool</text>
        <line x1="425" y1="290" x2="475" y2="290" stroke="#1a1814" stroke-width="1.25" marker-end="url(#arrowMuteG2)"/>

        <text x="500" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-weight="500" font-size="15" fill="#1a1814">Measure</text>
        <text x="500" y="298" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="1.5">tool</text>
        <line x1="525" y1="290" x2="575" y2="290" stroke="#1a1814" stroke-width="1.25" marker-end="url(#arrowMuteG2)"/>

        <text x="600" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Fraunces', serif" font-weight="500" font-size="15" fill="#1a1814">Decide</text>
        <text x="600" y="298" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" font-size="10" fill="#8a8680" letter-spacing="1.5">tool</text>

        <!-- HOOKS -->
